diff --git a/docs/evidence/vehicle-audio-continuity-2026-10-06/audition.html b/docs/evidence/vehicle-audio-continuity-2026-10-06/audition.html
new file mode 100644
--- /dev/null
+++ b/docs/evidence/vehicle-audio-continuity-2026-10-06/audition.html
@@ -0,0 +1,8 @@
+<!doctype html><html lang="en"><meta charset="utf-8"><meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1"><title>Beat my track — Continuous engine review</title>
+<style>body{margin:0;background:#101b27;color:#e9e3d7;font:17px/1.5 system-ui,sans-serif}main{max-width:820px;margin:48px auto;padding:0 24px}h1{font-size:34px;line-height:1.2}h2{margin:0 0 12px;font-size:22px;color:#ffd667}article{padding:20px;margin:16px 0;border:1px solid #344450;border-radius:12px;background:#182632}audio{width:100%}p{color:#b3bec5}article p{font-size:14px;margin:10px 0 0}a{color:#ffd667}small{color:#b3bec5}</style>
+<main><h1>Continuous engine review</h1><p>Corrected recordings from the actual Godot engine bus. Each twelve-second preview contains three seconds of idle, a smooth acceleration, six seconds of sustained revs across repeated loops, lift-off, then pause. Tire and impact sounds are excluded so the engine is easy to judge.</p><p>The resampling bug that inserted repeating silent gaps has been fixed. All 36 looped assets and all 15 captured idle/rev/lift-off segments pass continuity checks. The kart uses one gear. These are authored fictional engine voices, processed from cleared recordings. Hearing quality on the phone remains to be reviewed.</p><article><h2>Classic</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="classic-continuous.wav"></audio><p>Peak -9.7 dBFS · 0 clipped samples · silent paused tail</p></article>
+<article><h2>Compact</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="compact-continuous.wav"></audio><p>Peak -8.9 dBFS · 0 clipped samples · silent paused tail</p></article>
+<article><h2>Formula</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="formula-continuous.wav"></audio><p>Peak -7.9 dBFS · 0 clipped samples · silent paused tail</p></article>
+<article><h2>Kart</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="kart-continuous.wav"></audio><p>Peak -7.9 dBFS · 0 clipped samples · silent paused tail</p></article>
+<article><h2>Pickup</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="pickup-continuous.wav"></audio><p>Peak -7.5 dBFS · 0 clipped samples · silent paused tail</p></article><h2>Tire presence in the full mix</h2><p>The same held slide with engine and road sounds. The revised dry tire layer is 4.25 dB louder; grip/slip triggers are unchanged.</p><article><h2>Before</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="tires-before.wav"></audio></article><article><h2>After</h2><audio controls preload="metadata" src="tires-after.wav"></audio></article><small>No tire audio is present in these engine-only captures. General game tire credit: audible-edge (Tom Haigh), loop edit by qubodup, <a href="https://opengameart.org/content/car-tire-squeal-skid-loop">Car tire squeal skid loop</a>, <a href="https://creativecommons.org/licenses/by/3.0/">CC BY 3.0</a>. Resampled, filtered, looped and mastered. Other recorded masters: Nox Sound Design, Joseph SARDIN and DenisChardonnet (CC0). Full credits: game/assets/audio/vehicles/NOTICE.txt.</small></main>
+<script>const players=[...document.querySelectorAll('audio')];players.forEach(player=>player.addEventListener('play',()=>players.forEach(other=>{if(other!==player)other.pause()})))</script></html>
\ No newline at end of file
